### Link 1: https://www.contentstack.com/docs/headless-cms/live-preview-implementation-for-nextjs-csr-app-router

**Classification:** Vendor documentation (Contentstack) — **RELEVANT**

**Posted by:** Chenowa George on 2026-07-09, to understand "the gap/learning needed to implement the feature vs a POC"

**Document scope warning — ROUTER MISMATCH:**
The guide is titled "Live Preview Implementation for **NextJS CSR App Router**." The codebase uses **Pages Router** (files confirmed in `src/pages/`). Following this guide literally would be wrong for the codeline's architecture. A Pages Router equivalent guide should be sought, though the SDK contract may be similar.

**What the document says (quoted):**

On SDK installation — code changes ARE required:
> "Install and Initialize the Live Preview Utils SDK: Use the Live Preview Utils SDK to listen for content updates and fetch real-time preview data on the client side."
> `npm install @contentstack/live-preview-utils@contentstack/utils`

On the `onEntryChange` callback signature — it **takes a function argument**:
> `onEntryChange(updateData);`

The full pattern shown:
> ```js
> React.useEffect(() => {
>   onEntryChange(updateData);
>  }, []);
> ```

On SDK initialization — additional code required:
> ```js
> ContentstackLivePreview.init({
>   stackSdk: Stack,
>   enable: true,
>   ssr: false,
>   editButton: { enable: true },
>   stackDetails: { apiKey: "your api key", environment: "your environment value", branch: "your branch" },
>   clientUrlParams: { protocol: "https", host: "app.contentstack.com", port: 443 },
> });
> ```

On Delivery SDK configuration — also code:
> ```js
> live_preview: {
>   preview_token: preview_token,
>   enable: true,
>   host: 'rest-preview.contentstack.com'
>  },
> ```

On UI-side configuration — also required in Contentstack:
> "Navigate to Settings and select Environments. Set the base URLs for different locales, and click Update."
> "Select Visual Experience from the stack settings. In the General tab, select the Enable Live Preview checkbox. Set the Default Preview Environment and click Save."

On where Live Preview appears:
> "You can now see the Live Preview icon within all the entries of your stack and the feature previews data from the hosted website."

On Live Edit tags (recommended):
> "Live Edit tags allow editors to directly jump from the Live Preview pane to the corresponding content fields in the entry editor."

**CONTRADICTION with story assumption:**
- **Story says** (V-NandaKumar KR): "Its possible, no code changes are needed and its more of configure and use."
- **Document says**: Code changes are required — installing `@contentstack/live-preview-utils`, calling `ContentstackLivePreview.init()`, and wiring `onEntryChange(updateData)` into every page component. UI configuration is also needed but is not sufficient alone.

**CONTRADICTION with story assumption:**
- **Story says** (V-EPAM-Ivan Mikhailov): "The functionality is available only through the 'Visual experience' tab in Contentstack. It wont work from the Content type level (there is a 'Live preview' CTA) — Its a CS bug (TBD)"
- **Document says**: "You can now see the Live Preview icon within all the entries of your stack" — the doc describes Live Preview as accessible from entries, not limited to the Visual Experience tab. Whether this is a version discrepancy or a misunderstanding needs clarification from the Contentstack demo.

