### Link 2: https://www.contentstack.com/docs/headless-cms/custom-preview-urls#configure-custom-preview-urls

**Classification:** Vendor documentation (Contentstack) — **RELEVANT**

**Posted by:** V-EPAM-Ivan Mikhailov on 2026-07-27, as "Updated Contentstack docs link"

**What the document says (quoted):**

On what Custom Preview URLs are:
> "Custom Preview URLs allow you to define dynamic, pattern-based paths for Live Preview. These paths align preview behavior with your website's routing logic, including nested routes, taxonomies, multiple domains, and non-native URL fields."

On plan availability:
> "Custom Preview URLs is available on select plans. Contact Contentstack support for more information."

On configuration location — UI only, no code:
> "Go to your stack and click 'Settings'. Navigate to Visual Experience and select the Preview URL tab. Enable the Custom Preview URL toggle."

On URL pattern syntax:
> "Build preview URLs using dynamic placeholders in the pattern. Placeholders use the `{{...}}` syntax and can reference: Entry fields: `{{entry.slug}}`, `{{entry.title}}`, `{{entry.uid}}`; Context variables: `{{environment}}`, `{{locale}}`, `{{branch}}`, `{{contentTypeUid}}`; Reference fields: `{{entry.author.name}}`, `{{entry.parent.url}}`; Taxonomy values: `{{taxonomy:brand}}`"

On Visual Editor integration:
> "Custom Preview URLs resolve in Visual Editor the same way they do in Live Preview. After you configure a pattern under Settings → Visual Experience → Preview URL, Visual Editor uses that configuration to resolve entry URLs on the canvas. No additional setup is required."

On a code-side requirement for Visual Editor entry identification:
> "To open the correct entry, the Start editing button passes the entry UID and content type UID as page context. Configure this context once in your front-end code. For setup steps, refer to `setPageContext(context)` in the Live Preview Utils SDK config reference."

**Relevance to story:**
This doc addresses the team's concern about whether links/navigation will work inside Live Preview. Custom Preview URLs provide pattern-based routing for preview, which could address nested routes and multi-domain scenarios (GO, UP, MX). However, the `setPageContext` requirement means some front-end code is needed for Visual Editor integration.

